[h2][b]Installation[/b][/h2]

You can download the latest version via Steam client - [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3814885746]Dock Queue Indicator[/url]
Or you can do it via the Nexus Mods - [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/x4foundations/mods/2430]Dock Queue Indicator[/url]

[h2][b]Save state[/b][/h2]

[b]No[/b] (removing the extension does not break saves).

[h2][b]Usage[/b][/h2]

Open the map and the Property Owned list. Every station with ships waiting for a dock shows the queue icon with the count as the first icon of its row, before the docked-ships icon.

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/chemodun/X4-DockQueueIndicator/refs/heads/main/docs/images/stations_tab.png[/img]

Hover over the icon to see which ships are waiting.

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/chemodun/X4-DockQueueIndicator/refs/heads/main/docs/images/hover_queue.png[/img]

In Extension Options, under Dock Queue Indicator:
[list]
[*] [b]Show the dock queue size on station rows[/b] switches the icon on and off.
[*] [b]Green up to[/b] is the largest queue still shown in green.
[*] [b]Yellow up to[/b] is the largest queue shown in yellow; anything above is red.
[*] [b]Debug Level[/b] controls how much the mod writes to the game log.
[/list]
[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/chemodun/X4-DockQueueIndicator/refs/heads/main/docs/images/options.png[/img]

